\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The closest benchmark/evaluation surveys as a timeline. Two predate the recent wave, an IEEE\nonbreakingspace TETCI survey of embodied-AI simulators and tasks\nonbreakingspace \citep  {survey_embodiedsim} and a CoRL survey of real-robot RL reproducibility\nonbreakingspace \citep  {survey_rlrepro} (\textcolor {secD!55!black}{amber} = refereed venue); the rest are 2026 preprints on embodied evaluation, VLA data, and world models. None organises the robot-evaluation landscape by evaluation-mode $\times $ capability $\times $ model-family; the sole work reaching the advantage-of-prediction axis is a \emph  {position} paper\nonbreakingspace \citep  {pos_yangyu}. \textbf  {Ours} ($\star $) fills that cell; per-axis coverage is in Table\nonbreakingspace \ref {tab:survey_compare}.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:surveys}{{2}{3}{The closest benchmark/evaluation surveys as a timeline. Two predate the recent wave, an IEEE~TETCI survey of embodied-AI simulators and tasks~\cite {survey_embodiedsim} and a CoRL survey of real-robot RL reproducibility~\cite {survey_rlrepro} (\textcolor {secD!55!black}{amber} = refereed venue); the rest are 2026 preprints on embodied evaluation, VLA data, and world models. None organises the robot-evaluation landscape by evaluation-mode $\times $ capability $\times $ model-family; the sole work reaching the advantage-of-prediction axis is a \emph {position} paper~\cite {pos_yangyu}. \textbf {Ours} ($\star $) fills that cell; per-axis coverage is in Table~\ref {tab:survey_compare}.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
