\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Capability deep-dive}: the benchmarks that probe each of the $\beta $ capability cuts, and whether each builds a native VLA-vs-world-model contrast. Native contrasts cluster in the hidden-state, theory-of-mind and counterfactual \emph  {reasoning} cuts (LIBERO-Mem, ComPhy, AGENT, BIB, ACRE, CoPhy, CausalWorld); the long-horizon and social \emph  {task-success} cuts are largely model-agnostic (ALFWorld's abstract-to-grounded transfer is the lone partial). \textbf  {Eval}: \textcolor {magenta!80!black}{\textsf  {open}}/\textcolor {teal!80!black}{\textsf  {closed}}. \textbf  {VLA vs WM}: \textcolor {ForestGreen}{{\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 52}}\ native contrast, \textcolor {orange!90!black}{\textbf  {\textasciitilde }}\ partial, \textcolor {gray!65}{\textbf  {-{}-}}\ model-agnostic; each cut's header tallies the fraction of its benchmarks that build any (native or partial) contrast.\relax }}{12}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:compare_capability}{{5}{12}{Policy suites}{table.5}{}}
