\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The robot-evaluation benchmark landscape: 160 web-verified benchmarks, compared on four axes.} Grouped into four evaluation lanes and sub-grouped by capability. Columns: \textbf  {Year}; \textbf  {Capability} (what the benchmark stresses); \textbf  {Eval} (evaluation mode: open-loop prediction/generation quality, closed-loop task success, or a prediction-to-action bridge); and \textbf  {VLA vs WM} (does the benchmark build a native direct-policy vs world-model contrast: \textcolor {ForestGreen}{{\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 52}}\ explicit, \textcolor {orange!90!black}{\textbf  {\textasciitilde }}\ partial, \textcolor {gray!65}{\textbf  {-{}-}}\ model-agnostic). Every entry is a real, individually citeable benchmark.\relax }}{29}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:landscape}{{10}{29}{The full benchmark landscape}{table.10}{}}
